S 21900  Destinations are marked with waypoints. A waypoint appears as a purple diamond in your ship’s HUD, and it is also shown in your Contact List under the ‘Important’ filter.
         
         If the waypoint is offscreen, the purple diamond will appear at the edge of the screen. Turn in that direction to get it onscreen.
         
         Point your ship toward the waypoint and fly toward it.

S 21905  Make sure the waypointed Trade Lane ring is selected and then activate the DOCK maneuver.
         
         When selected, the ring has a distance indicator and is identified as ‘Planet Manhattan–>Fort Bush.’
         
         To select the ring:
         • Click on any part of the ring in space, or
         • Click on ‘Mission Waypoint’ in the Contact List in the bottom-left of your HUD.
         
         Then click the DOCK maneuver icon in the Neural Net at the top of your screen.

S 21910  Select the transport and then activate the FORMATION maneuver.
         
         To select the USV Brandt:
         • Click on any part of the ship in space, or
         • Click on ‘USV Brandt’ in the Contact List in the bottom-left of your HUD.
         
         Then click the FORMATION maneuver icon in the Neural Net at the top of your screen.

S 21915  Select the Pittsburgh docking ring and then activate the DOCK maneuver. To help you find the docking ring, the waypoint is currently marking that object.
         
         To select the docking ring:
         • Click on any part of the docking ring in space, or
         • Click on ‘Mission Waypoint’ in the Contact List in the bottom-left of your HUD.
         
         Then click the DOCK maneuver icon in the Neural Net at the top of your screen.

S 21920  Congratulations! You have advanced to Pilot Level 1.
         
         This new status allows you to purchase advanced equipment and ships that are appropriate to this level. In addition, you are now allowed to take on more difficult and profitable missions that require advanced pilot skills.

S 21925  New objectives in Freelancer are displayed for several seconds at the top of the screen. Objectives are automatically redisplayed every three minutes.
         
         OBJECTIVE COMMANDS:
         • N key – redisplay an objective.
         • F5 key or star icon at the top-right – view log of objectives and player journal.
         
         KEY SETTINGS:
         You can customize the default key settings by pressing F1, clicking Options, and then choosing Controls.

S 21930  When you are on a base or planet, a row of icons appears in the top-center of your screen that you can use to move to different locations. If you move your mouse over an icon, a tooltip will appear to identify it, and descriptive text will display in the top-left corner.
         
         ROOM COMMANDS:
         • Click on a character in the room – talk to him or her.
         • Click on the room icon (top row, top-center of screen) – move to that room.
         • Click on service icon (top-center of screen, bottom row) – use services in current
         \x2007\x200Aroom.

S 21935  PAUSING AND SAVING:
         Whenever you launch into space, the game updates the current Autosave. As you advance, the game will create progress-point saves and update the Autosave.
         • F1 key – pause the game and view the in-game menu.
         • F1 key and click Save Game – save the game when on a base or planet.
         • F1 key and click Load Game – load game.
         
         STATUS COMMANDS:
         • F6 key or grid icon in the top-right corner – open Nav Map of known locations.
         • F7 key or box icon – view and manipulate inventory.
         • F8 key or person icon – examine player status and reputation.
         • F9 or ‘i’ icon – read information on current location.

S 21940  SHIP MOVEMENT CONTROL:
         • FREE FLIGHT: Hold down the left mouse button and move your mouse in the
         \x2007\x200Adirection you want to turn.
         • MOUSE FLIGHT: Spacebar turns Mouse Flight on. Your ship now turns toward
         \x2007\x200Athe mouse cursor. To interact with the heads-up display, tap spacebar again.
         
         SHIP SPEED CONTROL:
         • W key accelerates your ship; S key decelerates your ship.
         • Tab key (held down) activates afterburner speed boost.
         
         COMBAT CONTROL:
         • Right mouse click fires active weapons; left mouse click on a target to select it.
         • R key selects the closest hostile target.

S 21945  When objects are destroyed, you can often salvage items from the wreckage.
         
         TRACTORING:
         • B or chest icon (to the right of speed indicator) – collect all nearby loot.
         • Shift-B – tractor selected loot.
         
         LOOTING TIPS:
         • Commodity loot can be sold on planets and bases for a profit.
         • Weapons and equipment loot can only be mounted on your ship when you are
         \x2007\x200Alanded on a base.
         • In mineable zones, shoot the small floating asteroids to find valuable commodities.
         • In remote locations, shoot abandoned vessels to obtain rare items.

S 21946  You have just experienced a Trade Lane attack. While fighting the enemy ships, your ship may take some damage.
         
         RECOVERING FROM DAMAGE:
         • F or circled-ship icon at the bottom-right – use shield batteries to help restore energy to shields.
         • G or wrench icon – repair hull damage with nanobots.

S 21947  You are now able to go anywhere in the New York solar system and accept missions as a freelancer. You need to increase your net worth to a set amount before Juni will contact you for the next mission. To view this amount, click on the Player Status icon (person icon, default key F8) in the top-right of your HUD.
         
         There are many ways to earn money. For example, you can complete a mission from a Job Board, mine asteroids, sell loot, or trade commodities.
         
         Don’t forget — since you don’t have jump access, you cannot leave the New York system at this time.

