S 60221  Trade Outpost
S 60222  A medium-sized base, usually a hub for goods and equipment traders.
S 60223  Gas Miner
S 60224  A station capable of mining valuable gases out of nebulae.
S 60225  Asteroid Miner
S 60226  Used for mining valuable minerals out of asteroid fields.
S 60227  Ice Asteroid Base
S 60228  A base built into a large ice asteroid.
S 60229  Asteroid Base
S 60230  A base built into a large asteroid.
S 60231  Shipyard
S 60232  An enormous structure used in the construction, maintenance, and repair of large ships.
S 60233  Telescope
S 60234  Used for peering deeper into space, it has both scientific and military applications.
S 60235  Communications Satellite
S 60236  A relay station for local and deep space communications.
S 60237  Gas Collector
S 60238  A unit used to capture space gases and dust for later refinement.
S 60239  HAZARD
S 60240  Unstable spatial anomaly.
S 60241  Solar Plant
S 60242  Solar energy collectors.
S 60243  Weapon Platform
S 60244  Heavily armed defense platform.
S 60245  Trade Lane Ring
S 60246  Trade lanes are used for superluminal travel within a system. Trade lanes must be entered from their origin point, usually located near key industrial, military, or civilian bases.
         
         The first trade lane was established through a joint venture between Deep Space Engineering and Ageira Technologies in the year 280 AS. By 350 AS, most of Liberty space was crisscrossed by trade lanes. Through financing from Interspace Commerce, the trade lane network was rapidly extended into the other colonies, helping to create a truly sector-wide economy. Trade lanes are the fastest and safest method of transporting goods and personnel within and between the colonies. Plans to expand the trade lanes to connect interests in the independent territories outside of the colonies are pending.

S 60247  Debris
S 60248  Debris object.
S 60249  Black Hole
S 60250  Remains of a collapsed star.
S 60251  Storage Tank
S 60252  Storage Tanks can contain fuel, water, or oxygen.
